    "### Set up the environment\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cell below to install and set up the kaggle environments:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "pip install --upgrade \"kaggle-environments>=1.32.2\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Then make sure to run `kaggle api enable` and `kaggle competitions register kaggriculture` to set up your Kaggle account.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "observation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Understanding the Observation\n",
    "\n",
    "Each turn your agent receives an observation with:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Field | Description |\n",
    "|-------|-------------|\n",
    "| player | Your player id (0 or 1) |\n",
    "| day | Current in-game day (0-indexed) |\n",
    "| hour | Turn within that day (0-indexed; there are 24 turns per day) |\n",
    "| farms | List of both players' public farm state, indexed by player id |\n",
    "| market | Shared inventory and current prices per product |\n",
    "| town | Shared unlocked_shops status |\n",
    "| private | Your own hidden state (not visible to opponent) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Farms** structure:\n",
    "- **money**: current bank balance\n",
    "- **tiles**: boardSize × boardSize grid indexed tiles[y][x]\n",
    "- **farmer**: [x, y] position of your main farmer\n",
    "- **hands**: [x, y] positions of any hired hands active today\n",
    "- **unlocked_quadrants**: subset of [\"NW\", \"NE\", \"SW\", \"SE\"]\n",
    "- **hires_today**: number of hires already made today\n",
    "\n",
    "**Private** state includes:\n",
    "- **shed**: counts of every product and animal\n",
    "- **seeds**: seed counts per crop\n",
    "- **inventories**: per-unit carried inventories\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tile types**:\n",
    "- **PLANT**: {kind: \"PLANT\", crop, planted_day, watered_today, consecutive_unwatered, yield_units, max_lifespan_step, fertilized_until_day}\n",
    "- **WEED**: {kind: \"WEED\"}\n",
    "- **COOP / PASTURE**: can be empty or occupied with animal data\n",
    "\n",
    "### Initial State Check\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this cell to see what the initial observation looks like:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "check-obs",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from kaggle_environments import make\n",
    "\n",
    "env = make(\"kaggriculture\", debug=True)\n",
    "env.run([\"random\", \"random\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Peek at the initial observation\n",
    "obs = env.steps[1][0].observation  # step 1 = first action step\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Player: {obs.player}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Board size: {len(obs.farms[obs.player]['tiles'])}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unlocked Farm Areas: {obs.farms[obs.player]['unlocked_quadrants']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMarket Prices:\")\n",
    "for item, price in obs.market.prices.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {item}: {price}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nUnlocked Town Shops: {obs.town.unlocked_shops}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "writefile",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Making a Submission\n",
    "\n",
    "You need to create a `submission.py` file (or `main.py`) with an `agent(obs)` function that returns actions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Three Ways to Submit:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Using the Kaggle UI**: Click \"Submit Agent\" and upload your file\n",
    "2. **Using Kaggle CLI**: \n",
    "   ```bash\n",
    "   kaggle competitions submit -c kaggriculture -p submission.py 1\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "3. **Using Notebook**: Upload `submission.py` or `submission.tar.gz` containing it\n",
    "\n",
    "### Agent Output Format\n",
    "\n",
    "Your agent must return a dict:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "{\"farmer\": action, \"hands\": [hand_action1, hand_action2, ...], \"market\": [market_action1, market_action2, ...]}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Farm Actions\n",
    "- `\"EAST\"`, `\"WEST\"`, `\"NORTH\"`, `\"SOUTH\"` - Move farmer/hand\n",
    "- `\"PLANT\"`, `\"WATER\"`, `\"HARVEST\"` - Act on current tile\n",
    "- `\"DIG\"` - Dig a weed\n",
    "- `\"CARE\"` - Care for coop/pasture\n",
    "- `\"FEED\"` - Feed animal in coop/pasture\n",
    "- `\"PASS\"` - Do nothing this turn\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Market Actions\n",
    "- `\"BUY_SEED\"`, `\"SELL\"`, `\"BUY_PRODUCT\"`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Market Price Updates\n",
    "\n",
    "Selling a product pushes its price down. Crops vary in how hard they crash from a glut:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Product | Supply Delta Price |\n",
    "|---------|-------------------|\n",
    "| WHEAT | Small crash |\n",
    "| CARROT | Medium crash |\n",
    "| TOMATO | Large crash |\n",
    "| STRAWBERRY | Very large crash |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Town Shops\n",
    "\n",
    "Shops open up over time and buy products, helping stabilize prices and prevent crashes.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "simple-agent",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Starter Agent: Melon Maxxer\n",
    "\n",
    "This first agent demonstrates the core concepts. It's a simple **melon-focused strategy**:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Buy melon seeds** when out of seeds and has cash\n",
    "2. **Plant melons** on empty tiles\n",
    "3. **Water melons** that need it\n",
    "4. **Harvest ripe melons** (when fully grown)\n",
    "5. **Sell melons** only when price >= threshold\n",
    "\n",
    "**Weaknesses**:\n",
    "- Only grows one crop (melons)\n",
    "- No farm hands (wasted opportunities)\n",
    "- No land expansion\n",
    "- No fertilization\n",
    "- Unsophisticated market timing (sells all at once)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "melon-maxxer",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from kaggle_environments.envs.kaggriculture.kaggriculture import CROPS\n",
    "\n",
    "# Game constants\n",
    "MELON_SEED_COST = CROPS[\"MELON\"][\"seed\"]\n",
    "MELON_MAX_YIELD_DAY = CROPS[\"MELON\"][\"max_yield_day\"]\n",
    "SELL_THRESHOLD = 200\n",
    "\n",
    "def _step_toward(fx, fy, tx, ty):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Determine direction to move toward target\"\"\"\n",
    "    if fx > tx:\n",
    "        return \"WEST\"\n",
    "    elif fx < tx:\n",
    "        return \"EAST\"\n",
    "    elif fy > ty:\n",
    "        return \"NORTH\"\n",
    "    elif fy < ty:\n",
    "        return \"SOUTH\"\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "def _find_target_tile(farm, board_size, have_seed):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Find the best target tile (harvest > water > plant)\"\"\"\n",
    "    fx, fy = farm[\"farmer\"]\n",
    "    candidates = []\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Scan all tiles\n",
    "    for y in range(board_size):\n",
    "        for x in range(board_size):\n",
    "            tile = farm[\"tiles\"][y][x]\n",
    "            \n",
    "            if isinstance(tile, dict) and tile.get(\"kind\") == \"PLANT\":\n",
    "                purpose = None\n",
    "                \n",
    "                # Harvest if ripe\n",
    "                age_ok = tile[\"yield_units\"] > 0\n",
    "                if age_ok and tile.get(\"planted_day\") is not None:\n",
    "                    purpose = \"harvest\"\n",
    "                \n",
    "                # Water if needed\n",
    "                if not tile[\"watered_today\"]:\n",
    "                    purpose = \"water\" if purpose is None else purpose\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if purpose:\n",
    "                    candidates.append((x, y, purpose))\n",
    "            elif tile is None and have_seed:\n",
    "                candidates.append((x, y, \"plant\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not candidates:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Sort: prioritize harvest > water > plant, then by distance\n",
    "    priority = {\"harvest\": 0, \"water\": 1, \"plant\": 2}\n",
    "    candidates.sort(key=lambda c: (priority[c[2]], abs(c[0] - fx) + abs(c[1] - fy)))\n",
    "    return candidates[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "def melon_maxxer(obs):\n",
    "    farms = obs.get(\"farms\", [])\n",
    "    player = obs.get(\"player\", 0)\n",
    "    private = obs.get(\"private\", {}) or {}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not farms or player >= len(farms):\n",
    "        return {\"farmer\": [\"PASS\"], \"hands\": [], \"market\": []}\n",
    "\n",
    "    farm = farms[player]\n",
    "    board_size = len(farm[\"tiles\"])\n",
    "    fx, fy = farm[\"farmer\"]\n",
    "    tile = farm[\"tiles\"][fy][fx]\n",
    "    day = obs.get(\"day\", 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    seeds = private.get(\"seeds\", {})\n",
    "    shed = private.get(\"shed\", {})\n",
    "    market_prices = (obs.get(\"market\", {}) or {}).get(\"prices\", {})\n",
    "    melon_price = market_prices.get(\"MELON\", 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    market = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Market actions: Sell melons only when price is good\n",
    "    melons_in_shed = shed.get(\"MELON\", 0)\n",
    "    if melons_in_shed > 0 and melon_price >= SELL_THRESHOLD:\n",
    "        market.append([\"SELL\", \"MELON\", melons_in_shed])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Top up seed inventory when empty and can afford\n",
    "    if seeds.get(\"MELON\", 0) == 0 and farm[\"money\"] >= MELON_SEED_COST:\n",
    "        market.append([\"BUY_SEED\", \"MELON\", 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Farmer action\n",
    "    farmer = [\"PASS\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if isinstance(tile, dict) and tile.get(\"kind\") == \"PLANT\" and tile[\"crop\"] == \"MELON\":\n",
    "        age = day - tile[\"planted_day\"]\n",
    "        if age >= MELON_MAX_YIELD_DAY and tile[\"yield_units\"] > 0:\n",
    "            farmer = [\"HARVEST\"]\n",
    "        elif not tile[\"watered_today\"]:\n",
    "            farmer = [\"WATER\"]\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            target = _find_target_tile(farm, board_size, seeds.get(\"MELON\", 0) > 0)\n",
    "            if target:\n",
    "                step = _step_toward(fx, fy, target[0], target[1])\n",
    "                if step:\n",
    "                    farmer = [step]\n",
    "    elif tile is None and seeds.get(\"MELON\", 0) > 0:\n",
    "        farmer = [\"PLANT\", \"MELON\"]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        target = _find_target_tile(farm, board_size, seeds.get(\"MELON\", 0) > 0)\n",
    "        if target:\n",
    "            step = _step_toward(fx, fy, target[0], target[1])\n",
    "            if step:\n",
    "                farmer = [step]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\"farmer\": farmer, \"hands\": [], \"market\": market}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "test-agent",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Test the melon_maxxer agent against random\n",
    "env = make(\"kaggriculture\", debug=True)\n",
    "env.run([melon_maxxer, \"random\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "final = env.steps[-1]\n",
    "for i, s in enumerate(final):\n",
    "    print(f\"Player {i}: reward={s.reward}, status={s.status}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# This is a very simple agent - it will likely lose to a smarter opponent\n",
    "# But it demonstrates the core loop!\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "next-steps",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What's Wrong with the Melon Maxxer?\n",
    "\n",
    "The starter agent has several problems:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Issue | Impact |\n",
    "|-------|--------|\n",
    "| Single crop only | Misses opportunities from other crops |\n",
    "| No farm hands | Wasted potential for parallel work |\n",
    "| No land expansion | Limited growing area |\n",
    "| No fertilization | Lower crop yields |\n",
    "| Naive market timing | Selling all at once crashes prices |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Next: Build Smarter Agents!\n",
    "\n",
    "Now you're ready to create your own strategies. Consider these improvements:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Multi-Crop Management\n",
    "- Track multiple crops (wheat, carrots, tomatoes, etc.)\n",
    "- Plant based on current market prices\n",
    "- Balance production across different products\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Farm Hand Optimization\n",
    "- Hire hands when beneficial\n",
    "- Assign tasks strategically (watering, harvesting, caring for animals)\n",
    "- Manage hand costs vs. productivity\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Market Timing\n",
    "- Wait for prices to rise before selling\n",
    "- Use town shops to stabilize prices\n",
    "- Sell in smaller batches to avoid crashes\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4. Resource Management\n",
    "- Buy and use fertilizer strategically\n",
    "- Care for animals to prevent escape\n",
    "- Expand land efficiently\n",
    "\n",
    "## Submissions\n",
    "\n",
    "Save your agent in a `submission.py` file and submit to the competition!\n"
   ]
  }
